# nl-memory-1: the first-start downloads of the memory runtime are shown (desktop side)

The core now raises a `notice` section entry (key `memory-runtime:database` or `memory-runtime:embedding`,
code `memory-runtime-preparing`, params `{ stage: "database" | "embedding" }`) while the PostgreSQL runtime or the
embedding model downloads, and removes it when the download ends. The renderer ignores an unknown code, so nothing shows
until this is applied.

1. apps/desktop/src/shared/desktop-notice.ts: add `'memory-runtime-preparing',` to DESKTOP_NOTICE_CODES (after 'offload-prune-blocked').
2. apps/desktop/src/renderer/desktop-toasts.tsx, desktopNoticeToast: add a case after 'offload-prune-blocked':

    case 'memory-runtime-preparing':
      return {
        text:
          notice.params.stage === 'embedding'
            ? t('Downloading the memory search model for the first time. This can take a few minutes.')
            : t('Downloading the memory database for the first time. This can take a few minutes.'),
        tone: 'info',
      };

3. apps/desktop/src/renderer/locales/*.json (de, es, fr, it, ja, ko, pt-BR, ru, vi): add the two English keys above with their translations
   (the locale test requires every t() key in every locale).
